          "check": "tier_integrity",
          "severity": "warning",
          "detail": "The claim citing E20 is marked 'measurable' but the Urban Transport Group is an advocacy/interest body. The figures may be well-founded but without an independent institutional source, this is at best 'projected'. Not blocking given low weight in the overall verdict, but the tier is overstated."
        }
      ],
      "notes": "The verdict is broadly well-constructed. Direction 'mixed' is genuinely supported by claims on both sides: upside (IFS benefit-cost ratio, regional connectivity gains) and downside (NAO seat reductions, additionality dispute, delivery risk). The 'stated' tier claims for regional allocations use E3 which only quotes the North figure; Midlands and Rest of Country figures are asserted but only E3 is cited \u2014 minor gap but not blocking since the broader allocation is corroborated across multiple evidence units. The E24 CPA source is commercial/industry advocacy and is correctly used only as one projected voice among several, not as a sole basis. The rationale is party-blind and does not impute motive. Magnitude 'moderate' and confidence 'low' are defensible given genuine uncertainty over additionality and delivery. No blocking issues found."
    },
